<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuel Bulnes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1799–1866</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Manuel Bulnes Prieto</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manuel Bulnes was a Chilean general and president. He commanded the army that won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-yungay">Battle of Yungay</a> in 1839, destroying the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>–Bolivian Confederation, and served two terms as president from 1841 to 1851. His government founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-chile">University of Chile</a>, took possession of the Strait of Magellan and encouraged immigration and education.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manuel-bulnes.jpg" alt="Manuel Bulnes" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raymond Monvoisin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ManuelBulnes.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
